{"id":"VHH__LightBox__compounds__LB_skydome","collection":"VHH","category":"LightBox/compounds","source_path":"VHH/LightBox/compounds/LB_skydome.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::LB_skydome"],"counts":{"nodes":54,"connections":102,"values":35,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Skydome - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a skydome light. It does this by taking the direction to each point in the \"dome\" (a sphere generated based on input) and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity.","documentation_search":"LB skydome Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Skydome - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a skydome light. It does this by taking the direction to each point in the \"dome\" (a sphere generated based on input) and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity. The diagnostic tab will hide and show the dome generated sphere. Input input mesh The object you are lighting. enable skydome An \"on/off\" switch for the domelight contribution, when this is checked, the compound will output the resulting values for the domelight to be added to the lighting. dome radius The radius of the dome. This should be considerably larger than the object you are lighting. ground The color at the bottom of the domelight. sky horizon The color at the middle of the domelight. sky zenith The color at the top of the domelight. intensity The overall brightness of the domelight. horizon bias Adjusts the position of the dome's horizon. dome resolution The number of points to calculate the domelight lighting from, the higher the number, the smoother the lighting, but the heavier the calculation. weight This is an overall multiplier of the output. It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of float , floatArray and scalar field data. black array This port is intended for use in the LightBox system. It is an array of value {0,0,0} that the light result will be added to, can be left unconnected. Output skydome contribution An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting. Add this to the point color of your mesh to see the result. light data An object carrying the light data - this is intended for use with the LB display compound.","port_names":["black_array","dome_radius","dome_resolution","enable_skydome","ground","horizon_bias","input_mesh","intensity","light_data","sky_horizon","sky_zenith","skydome_contribution","skydome_weight"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_bounds","Core::Array::array_is_empty","Core::Array::array_size","Core::Array::find_all_in_array","Core::Array::get_from_array","Core::Array::resize_array","Core::Array::set_in_array","Core::Conversion::vector3_to_scalar","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Graph::terminal","Core::Logic::greater","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::change_range","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::dot","Core::Math::lerp","Core::Math::max","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::normalize","Core::Object::set_property","Core::Type_Conversion::to_float","Core::Type_Conversion::to_int","Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material","Geometry::Common::interpret_auto_port_as_scalar","Geometry::Mesh::get_mesh_structure","Geometry::Properties::get_point_count","Geometry::Properties::get_point_normal","Geometry::Properties::get_point_position","Geometry::Properties::set_point_normal","Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere","Unknown","apply_lighting","check_the_black_array_input","color_the_dome","create_the_skydome","light_equation"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::LB_skydome","uri_imported":"file:///LB_skydome.json","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/LB_skydome.md"},"documentation_file":"VHH/LightBox/docs/LB_skydome.md","documentation":"### ***LB_skydome***\n**Component Compound** - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system.<br /><br />\n**Skydome** - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a *skydome* light.  It does this by taking the direction to each point in the \"dome\" (a sphere generated based on input) and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity.<br /><br />\nThe diagnostic tab will hide and show the dome generated sphere.<br />\n\n***\n\n## Input\n\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***input_mesh***</span>\n<br />The object you are lighting. \n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***enable_skydome***</span>\n<br />An \"on/off\" switch for the domelight contribution, when this is checked, the compound will output the resulting values for the domelight to be added to the lighting. \n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***dome_radius***</span>\n<br />The radius of the dome.  This should be considerably larger than the object you are lighting.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***ground***</span>\n<br />The color at the bottom of the domelight.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***sky_horizon***</span>\n<br />The color at the middle of the domelight.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***sky_zenith***</span>\n<br />The color at the top of the domelight.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***intensity***</span>\n<br />The overall brightness of the domelight.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***horizon_bias***</span>\n<br />Adjusts the position of the dome's horizon.\n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***dome_resolution***</span>\n<br />The number of points to calculate the domelight lighting from, the higher the number, the smoother the lighting, but the heavier the calculation.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***weight***</span>\n<br />This is an overall multiplier of the output.  It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of `float`, `floatArray` and `scalar_field` data.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***black_array***</span>\n<br />This port is intended for use in the LightBox system.  It is an array of value {0,0,0} that the light result will be added to, can be left unconnected. \n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***skydome_contribution***</span>\n<br />An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting.  Add this to the `point_color` of your mesh to see the result. \n\n<span style=\"color:#90A3F4\">***light_data***</span>\n<br />An object carrying the light data - this is intended for use with the `LB_display` compound.","ports":[{"name":"input_mesh","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"dome_radius","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"600f"},{"name":"ground","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0.0769999996f","y":"0.0367644988f","z":"0.00138599996f"}},{"name":"sky_horizon","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0.800000012f","y":"0.800000012f","z":"0.800000012f"}},{"name":"sky_zenith","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0.50849998f","y":"0.648699999f","z":"0.929099977f"}},{"name":"intensity","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.25f"},{"name":"horizon_bias","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0f"},{"name":"dome_resolution","direction":"input","type":"int","default":"30L"},{"name":"skydome_weight","direction":"input","type":null,"default":"1f"},{"name":"enable_skydome","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"true"},{"name":"black_array","direction":"input","type":"array<Math::float3>"},{"name":"light_data","direction":"output","type":"Object"},{"name":"skydome_contribution","direction":"output","type":"array<Math::float3>"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}],"counts":{"nodes":54,"connections":102,"values":35,"nested_compounds":6},"node_types":{"Core::Math::multiply":5,"Unknown":4,"Core::Type_